{"title":"Career roadmap · Planning Assistant","role":"Planning Assistant","summary":"A Planning Assistant supports urban, regional, infrastructure, transport, environmental or community-planning teams by collecting and analysing spatial and demographic information, preparing maps and reports, maintaining planning databases, assisting with surveys and supporting planners in preparing development proposals.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Planning Assistant supports urban, regional, infrastructure, transport, environmental or community-planning teams by collecting and analysing spatial and demographic information, preparing maps and reports, maintaining planning databases, assisting with surveys and supporting planners in preparing development proposals."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA Geography provides a strong foundation in human geography, physical geography, population, settlements, economic geography, regional development and spatial analysis. To become employable in planning, this should be combined with GIS, remote sensing, statistics, urban/regional planning concepts, CAD and planning-data analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Geography graduate, the strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Geography","GIS + Planning Skills","Planning Internship","Planning/GIS Assistant","Planning Specialist","Planner/Planning Manager"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A Planning Assistant can be an entry/support role, but statutory or professional Town Planner/Urban Planner positions may require a recognised postgraduate planning qualification or specific professional eligibility. A BA Geography should not be presented as universally sufficient for independent statutory planning practice."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"